---
/*
 * Privacy Policy & Terms (DIG-80). Replaces the conversion spec 3.6
 * launch default. Source copy: the copy-master document on DIG-80,
 * revision 5 — revision 3 (approved DIG-103 draft with the DIG-104
 * fact-check and DIG-119 compliance-review fixes, and the owner's
 * question-card answers inserted, 2026-10-20), plus revision 5: the six
 * company-protective terms clauses from the DIG-130 wording pass as
 * validated by DIG-131, and the PAIA manual statement removed after the
 * owner's decision of 2026-10-21 (F10 recorded as an accepted risk).
 *
 * Constraints from the issue: keep noindex; keep the URL /privacy.
 * The /privacy-policy/ 301 belongs to the redirect task (DIG-18).
 */
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
import { site, legal } from '../lib/site.config';
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Privacy Policy & Terms"
  description="How Digitally Shifted handles personal information on digitallyshifted.com under POPIA, and the terms that apply to your use of this site."
  path="/privacy"
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  meta="Last updated 21 October 2026"
  noindex={true}
>
  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Digitally Shifted is a digital agency. We operate the website
    digitallyshifted.com. We operate in South Africa. Under the Protection of
    Personal Information Act (POPIA), we are the responsible party for the
    personal information that this website collects.
  </p>
  <p>
    Digitally Shifted is the trading name of {legal.legalName}, a private
    company registered in South Africa.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Registration number: {legal.registrationNumber}</li>
    <li>Registered office: {legal.registeredOffice}</li>
    <li>Director: {legal.director}</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Contact us about privacy in these ways:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`} class="link-dark">{site.email}</a>
    </li>
    <li>Phone and WhatsApp: {site.phoneDisplay}</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. What personal information we collect</h2>
  <p>
    We collect personal information when you send us an enquiry or a quote
    request through our forms. We collect only the information listed in this
    section. Our forms collect:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name (required)</li>
    <li>
      Your email address or your phone number. Give at least one, so that we
      can reply to you
    </li>
    <li>The option that you pick from the &ldquo;What do you need?&rdquo; list (required)</li>
    <li>Your business name (optional)</li>
    <li>Your message (required)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You do not have to fill in the optional fields. The form works without
    them. Your message gives us the details of your enquiry. We do not
    knowingly collect personal information from children.
  </p>
  <p>
    The form record also stores the date and time and a submission ID. For
    spam control and rate limiting, the form record stores a salted hash of
    your IP address. The form record does not store your raw IP address.
  </p>
  <p>Our analytics tool also collects website usage data. Section 4 describes this data.</p>

  <h2>3. Why we process it and on what basis</h2>
  <p>We process your personal information for these purposes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>To reply to your enquiry</li>
    <li>To prepare the quote that you request</li>
    <li>To keep the site secure through spam control and rate limiting</li>
    <li>To measure how people use the site through analytics</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We process this information only for these purposes. Each purpose has a
    lawful basis under section 11 of POPIA:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Your consent is the basis for the details that you give us in the form.
      You give this consent when you submit the form. You can withdraw it at
      any time (section 8 of this policy).
    </li>
    <li>
      Your request is the basis for using your details to reply to you and to
      prepare your quote. These are steps that we take at your request before
      a possible contract (section 11(1)(b) of POPIA).
    </li>
    <li>
      Our legitimate interest is the basis for spam control, rate limiting,
      and analytics. The interest is a secure website that works well
      (section 11(1)(f) of POPIA).
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>The form includes a consent line. It reads:</p>
  <blockquote>
    <p>We use your details to reply to this enquiry. We do not sell them.</p>
  </blockquote>
  <p>This policy gives you more detail. You can read it before you submit the form.</p>

  <h2>4. Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We use Google Analytics 4 (GA4) to measure this website. GA4 measures page
    views and button clicks. The button clicks include calls, WhatsApp clicks,
    and form submissions. This data shows us which pages and buttons people
    use.
  </p>
  <p>
    GA4 uses cookies or similar identifiers for this measurement. Cookies are
    small files that a website can store on your device. At launch, this site
    sends no advertising trackers.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Who receives personal information</h2>
  <p>We do not sell your personal information. We share it only with the service providers that operate this website for us:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Our hosting provider</li>
    <li>Our form backend</li>
    <li>Google, for Analytics</li>
    <li>Our email delivery service</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These providers are operators under POPIA. They process personal
    information only for us and on our instructions. When you submit a form,
    one notification email goes to {site.email}. The notification email
    contains the details of your submission. We send no automatic marketing
    email.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Storage, security safeguards, and how long we keep records</h2>
  <p>
    We keep personal information only as long as we need it for the purposes
    in section 3. Section 14 of POPIA controls this. We may keep a record
    longer only if the law requires or authorises it, if we reasonably need it
    for lawful purposes related to our functions or activities, if a contract
    requires it, or if you consented. When we may no longer keep a record, we
    destroy or delete it, or de-identify it, as soon as reasonably
    practicable, in a way that prevents reconstruction (sections 14(4) and
    (5) of POPIA).
  </p>
  <p>Our analytics provider keeps website usage data for 14 months.</p>
  <p>
    As a guide, we keep enquiry records for 24 months after our last contact
    with you, unless the law requires us to keep them longer or you ask us to
    remove them sooner.
  </p>
  <p>
    We keep enquiry records until you ask us to remove them. We also remove
    enquiry records when we no longer need them for the purposes in section 3.
    Enquiry records include the form fields described in section 2.
  </p>
  <p>You can ask us to remove your records at any time. Send your request to {site.email}.</p>
  <p>
    We apply reasonable security safeguards to protect the personal
    information that we hold. If a security compromise affects your personal
    information, we notify the Information Regulator and you when POPIA
    section 22 requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Cross-border processing</h2>
  <p>
    Our analytics provider may process data outside South Africa. Section 72
    of POPIA sets the conditions for transfers of personal information outside
    South Africa. We will transfer your personal information outside South
    Africa only if the recipient is bound by law, binding corporate rules, or
    a binding agreement that gives adequate protection, or if you consented,
    or if the transfer is necessary for a contract with you or in your
    interest, or if the transfer is for your benefit where we cannot
    reasonably get your consent.
  </p>
  <p>
    The analytics provider is Google, as described in section 4. Google
    processes this data for us and on our instructions. Google is bound by a
    data processing agreement for Analytics.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Your rights under POPIA</h2>
  <p>POPIA gives you rights over your personal information. You can:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Ask us to confirm whether we hold personal information about you, and
      ask for access to the record or a description of it, including the third
      parties who have had access (section 23 of POPIA)
    </li>
    <li>
      Ask us to correct or delete information that is inaccurate, irrelevant,
      excessive, out of date, incomplete, misleading, or obtained unlawfully,
      or to destroy or delete a record that we may no longer keep (section 24
      of POPIA)
    </li>
    <li>
      Object, at any time, to our processing of your personal information. If
      you object, we may no longer process your information (sections 11(3)
      and 11(4) of POPIA). You can object on Form 1 of the POPIA Regulations,
      available from the Information Regulator
    </li>
    <li>Withdraw your consent to processing</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To use a right, send an email to {site.email}. Tell us which right you
    want to use. Describe the information or the change that you want. We will
    respond to your request within 30 days.
  </p>
  <p>
    If we ever send direct marketing by electronic communication, we will do
    it only as section 69 of POPIA allows: with your consent, or to you as an
    existing customer for our own similar services, with a free way to object
    in every message.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you believe that we have interfered with the protection of your
    personal information, you can submit a complaint to the Information
    Regulator (South Africa) under section 74 of POPIA (read with sections 73
    and 75). The Information Regulator enforces POPIA. Its website is
    <a href="https://inforegulator.org.za/" class="link-dark" rel="noopener">inforegulator.org.za</a>.
    You can complain through its eServices Portal
    (<a href="https://eservices.inforegulator.org.za/" class="link-dark" rel="noopener">eservices.inforegulator.org.za</a>)
    or by email to POPIAComplaints@inforegulator.org.za.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Access to other records under the Promotion of Access to Information Act (PAIA)</h2>
  <p>
    PAIA gives you a way to request access to certain records that we hold. To
    request access to a record, send your request to our Information Officer
    in the prescribed form (section 53 of PAIA).
  </p>
  <p>
    Our Information Officer is {legal.informationOfficer}. Send your request
    to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`} class="link-dark">{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes to this policy and the effective date</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. We publish every change on
    this page. You can check this page for the current version. This policy
    and these terms take effect on the day that this page goes live.
  </p>

  <h2 id="terms">Terms &amp; Conditions</h2>

  <h2>Agreement to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    These terms apply to your use of digitallyshifted.com. When you use this
    site, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree with these terms, do
    not use the site.
  </p>
  <p>If we do not enforce a term, we do not lose the right to enforce it later.</p>

  <h2>What the site is for</h2>
  <p>
    This site gives information about Digitally Shifted and our services. You
    can use our forms to send us an enquiry. Our services are:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Launch</li>
    <li>Care plan</li>
    <li>Custom builds</li>
    <li>Social Media Marketing</li>
    <li>Paid Ads</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    This site does not promise any result from these services. We may change,
    pause, or close the site, or any part of it, at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Our content is not advice</h2>
  <p>
    Content on this site is general information about our services. It is not
    legal, financial, or other professional advice. Get advice from a
    qualified professional before you make a decision.
  </p>

  <h2>Enquiries and quotes are invitations to enquire</h2>
  <p>
    Content on this site and any quote that we send are invitations to
    enquire. They are not binding offers. An engagement with us starts only
    when we sign an agreement with you.
  </p>

  <h2>Intellectual property in the site content</h2>
  <p>
    Digitally Shifted owns the content on this site. The content includes the
    text, design, logos, and images. You may read this content and share links
    to it. You may not copy, change, or republish it without our written
    permission.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use of the site</h2>
  <p>Use this site lawfully and respectfully. Do not:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Send spam or harmful content through our forms</li>
    <li>Try to gain unauthorized access to the site or its systems</li>
    <li>Interfere with the operation of the site</li>
    <li>Use the site in a way that harms us or other people</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you breach these terms, we may suspend or end your access to the site.</p>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    The site may link to other websites. We do not control those websites. We
    are not responsible for their content or their privacy practices. Read
    the terms and privacy policy of any website that you visit.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability and no warranty</h2>
  <p>
    These terms cover this website only. They do not cover client
    engagements. Client engagements run under separate signed agreements.
  </p>
  <p>
    We provide this site as is, without warranties of any kind. We do not
    promise that the site will be available or free of errors.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>
      We limit our liability for loss or damage from your use of the site only
      to the extent that the law permits. Nothing in these terms excludes
      liability that we cannot lawfully exclude. This includes liability for
      gross negligence.
    </strong>
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    South African law governs these terms and any dispute that relates to
    them. The South African courts have jurisdiction over disputes about these
    terms.
  </p>

  <h2>If part of these terms is invalid</h2>
  <p>If a court finds part of these terms invalid, the remaining terms stay in force.</p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms and how to contact us</h2>
  <p>
    We may change these terms from time to time. We publish every change on
    this page. Your continued use of the site after a change means that you
    accept the changed terms.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you have a question about these terms, contact us at
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`} class="link-dark">{site.email}</a>.
  </p>
</ContentLayout>
